        "node_id": "n_7_773458",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-2: Ensure that when multiple rude passengers are equidistant from a seat, only the first one to reach that seat actually occupies it, preventing simultaneous attempts and subsequent explosions. This can be achieved by processing the queue in a way that respects the order of arrival, ensuring that only the first occupant of a seat remains, and others continue searching for the next available seat.",
