        "node_id": "n_5_5ad602",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (revised): Instead of using BFS to find the shortest path for each person individually, use a single BFS traversal to identify all reachable seats from each person simultaneously. This approach ensures that we efficiently determine the minimum distances for all persons in a single pass, reducing the overall complexity and avoiding potential timeouts.",
